  "text": "She said yes to the impossible, and the world turned. Luke chapter one. Gabriel is sent to Nazareth, to a virgin espoused to a man named Joseph, and her name is Mary. Note what Luke tells us and what he does not. He gives us the town, the man she is promised to, his royal line. He never gives us her age. So when you hear her called a teenager, that is tradition talking, not the text. The angel says, Hail, thou that art highly favoured, the Lord is with thee. And she is troubled. Not by the angel. By the greeting. She is turning the words over, wondering what kind of salutation this is. Then the news. You will conceive and bear a son, and call his name Jesus, and his kingdom will have no end. She asks one practical question. How shall this be, seeing I know not a man? She is not asking for proof. She is asking how. And when the answer comes, she says, Behold the handmaid of the Lord, be it unto me according to thy word. She said yes to a plan she could not verify, in a village that could count.",
